<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆδος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>,
			τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέδω</span>) poet.
		Noun, only in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήδεα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>counsels, plans, arts</i>, mostly
			with collat. notion of <i>prudence</i> or <i>cunning</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλους καὶ μ. πυκνά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.202
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλαὶ . . μ. τ᾽ ἀνδρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.340
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεπνυμένα μ. εἰδώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.278
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυκινὰ φρεσὶ μ. ἔχοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.674
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖς ἐναλίγκια μ. ἔχοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.89
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχης μ.</span>
			<i>plans</i> of fight, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.467
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.120
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. πατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					398
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήδεσιν ἀμοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.27
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				10.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικότοισι μήδεσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					601
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σός τε πόθος σά τε
			μ.</span> longing for thee and thy <i>counsels</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.202
			</span></i>.</div>
